---
{#- Open fridge desserts sign (client 2026-11-06): the second dessert
    fridge stands out in the open, and it is not self serve. `fridgeKinds`
    above are the kinds on it, by their name in Square, in this order, each
    at its item's price in Square (src/_data/desserts.json, see
    sign-desserts-bw.njk). They show even when Square counts them at 0: the
    sign is for what that fridge holds, not today's stock. A kind not in
    Square at all is left off. If you find yourself typing a price here,
    stop. -#}
{%- set rows = [] %}
{%- for name in fridgeKinds %}
{%- for item in desserts.items %}
{%- for k in item.kinds %}
{%- if k.name == name %}
{%- set _ = rows.push({ name: name, price: item.price }) %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- set triangle %}
<svg class="dc-icon" viewBox="0 0 100 88" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 5 L95 83 H5 Z" fill="#fff" stroke="#000" stroke-width="8" stroke-linejoin="round"/><rect x="45" y="30" width="10" height="30" rx="4" fill="#000"/><circle cx="50" cy="71" r="6" fill="#000"/></svg>
{%- endset %}
<div class="canvas sign sign--bw fd dc">
    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title">Desserts</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="sign-rows fd-rows">
        {%- for r in rows %}
        <li class="sign-row">
            <div class="sign-row-head">
                <span class="sign-row-name">{{ r.name }}</span>
                <span class="sign-row-fill" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="sign-row-price">{{ r.price | money }}</span>
            </div>
        </li>
        {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    <section class="dc-caution">
        <div class="dc-caution-inner">
            {{ triangle | safe }}
            <div class="dc-words">
                <p class="p-display dc-title">Not self serve</p>
                <p class="dc-sub">Please do not open.<br>Ask at the counter.</p>
            </div>
            {{ triangle | safe }}
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
